MORE CONNECTED

226
00:08:39,986 --> 00:08:41,520
IN THAT YOU DIED TWICE.

227
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:43,222
Ann: (laughs)

228
00:08:43,222 --> 00:08:46,659
Sande: SO I THINK
WE HAVE A WINNER.

229
00:08:46,659 --> 00:08:48,128
Norelle: SHE FORGOT NICOLE.

230
00:08:48,128 --> 00:08:50,363
I, SERIOUSLY, WAS LIKE...

231
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:51,364
Sande: NICOLE?
DO WE HAVE NICOLE?

232
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:52,632
Taye: YES.
Sande: NICOLE.

233
00:08:52,632 --> 00:08:54,134
Nicole: OUCH.

234
00:08:54,134 --> 00:08:55,635
OH, THAT'S NOT GOOD.

235
00:08:55,635 --> 00:08:58,171
Taye: I THOUGHT YOU WERE
VERY SENSITIVE, VERY, VERY--

236
00:08:58,171 --> 00:08:59,272
WHICH IS A GREAT THING.

237
00:08:59,272 --> 00:09:00,974
Sande: AND WE HAVE
A WINNER NOW.

238
00:09:00,974 --> 00:09:05,378
INSTEAD OF TELLING YOU,
WATCH THAT SCREEN.

239
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:09,049
>> Yaya: THE PROGNOSIS...

240
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:11,017
Nicole: SO YAYA WINS AGAIN.

241
00:09:11,017 --> 00:09:12,519
>> Taye: NURSE!

242
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:20,560
Taye: NURSE, WHAT AM I
GONNA DO WITHOUT MY BABY?

243
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,429
Tyra: I THINK YOU MIGHT WANT
TO TAKE A LOOK AT HER CHART.

244
00:09:22,429 --> 00:09:24,697
Taye: BEFORE I LOOK
AT HER CHART, CAN I HAVE A HUG?

245
00:09:24,697 --> 00:09:26,566
Tyra: DR. DIGGS.

246
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:27,600
Taye: WHAT'S GOIN' ON
WITH THIS CHART?

247
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,669
Tyra: IT SHOULD TELL US
EVERYTHING.

248
00:09:29,669 --> 00:09:33,273
Taye: OKAY, IT SAYS HERE,
"YOU'VE TAKEN YOUR CLASS.

249
00:09:33,273 --> 00:09:35,708
YOU'VE BEEN CHALLENGED BY ME,
BUT NOW IT'S TIME

250
00:09:35,708 --> 00:09:37,477
TO ACT FOR TV."

251
00:09:37,477 --> 00:09:39,179
Tyra: "IT'S NOT
GONNA BE EASY.

252
00:09:39,179 --> 00:09:40,980
YOU'LL BE ON THE GO.

253
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:44,651
SO PACK YOUR BAGS, GIRLS,
BECAUSE YOU'RE GOIN' TO TOKYO!"

254
00:09:44,651 --> 00:09:47,353
All: (yelling)

255
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:49,422
Eva: OH, MY GOD.

256
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:50,723
I CANNOT BELIEVE--LIKE,

257
00:09:50,723 --> 00:09:53,460
IT'S ONE OF THE FASHION CAPITALS
OF THE WORLD.

258
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:56,496
LIKE, TOKYO--THEY HAVE
THE ILLEST, SICKEST STYLE

259
00:09:56,496 --> 00:09:57,697
THERE IS.

260
00:09:57,697 --> 00:10:01,201
Tyra: THE WINNER OF THIS
HAS AN AMAZING PRIZE.

261
00:10:01,201 --> 00:10:05,138
YOU WILL BE FLYING TO TOKYO
IN LUXURY CLASS.

262
00:10:05,138 --> 00:10:06,606
Taye: OOH.

263
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:10,009
Tyra: AND YOU HAVE TO CHOOSE
ONE OF THESE GIRLS

264
00:10:10,009 --> 00:10:12,178
TO COME WITH YOU.

265
00:10:12,178 --> 00:10:16,049
AND THE REST
WILL BE IN THE BACK IN COACH

266
00:10:16,049 --> 00:10:18,518
FOR 13 HOURS.

267
00:10:18,518 --> 00:10:20,086
Yaya: AMANDA, WOULD YOU
LIKE TO ACCOMPANY ME?

268
00:10:20,086 --> 00:10:21,521
Amanda: YEAH!

269
00:10:21,521 --> 00:10:23,289
Yaya: THIS IS MY FOURTH
CONSECUTIVE WIN,

270
00:10:23,289 --> 00:10:24,991
SO I PICKED NICOLE ONCE.

271
00:10:24,991 --> 00:10:25,992
I PICKED NORELLE.

272
00:10:25,992 --> 00:10:27,093
IT WAS AMANDA'S TURN.

273
00:10:27,093 --> 00:10:28,161
Taye: BEST OF LUCK.

274
00:10:28,161 --> 00:10:29,629
BEST OF LUCK.

275
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,464
ALL RIGHT,
ALL RIGHT, Y'ALL.

276
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:32,465
Yaya: TOKYO!

277
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:34,033
Amanda: I'M
KIND OF SPEECHLESS,

278
00:10:34,033 --> 00:10:39,005
'CAUSE I'VE NEVER BEEN TO TOKYO,
AND IT'S GONNA BE INSANE.

279
00:10:39,005 --> 00:10:40,273
All: (talking at once)

280
00:10:51,384 --> 00:10:52,418
Eva: OH!

281
00:10:52,418 --> 00:10:55,088
WE'RE GOIN' TO TOKYO!

282
00:10:55,088 --> 00:10:58,158
GOTTA PACK UP THE LITTLE SNACKS,
LADIES.

283
00:10:58,158 --> 00:11:00,727
YOU'RE GOIN' TO TOKYO.

284
00:11:00,727 --> 00:11:02,262
Ann: FROM WHAT I UNDERSTAND,
IT'S NEW YORK

285
00:11:02,262 --> 00:11:03,496
TO THE TENTH POWER.

286
00:11:03,496 --> 00:11:05,298
LIKE, JUST CRAZINESS.

287
00:11:07,367 --> 00:11:09,369
Norelle: I'M NERVOUS
ABOUT THE WHOLE TOKYO SITUATION.

288
00:11:09,369 --> 00:11:11,004
I HEAR THAT--I DON'T KNOW WHAT
THEY CALL THEM--

289
00:11:11,004 --> 00:11:13,606
JAPANESE PEOPLE FROM TOKYO
OR "TOKYANS."

290
00:11:15,074 --> 00:11:16,075
Ann: I DON'T WANNA FLY.

291
00:11:16,075 --> 00:11:17,577
I'M REALLY SCARED.

292
00:11:17,577 --> 00:11:19,679
Norelle: WHAT'S WRONG?
Ann: I HATE THIS.

293
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:21,414
I DON'T LIKE FLYING, AND I DID
HAVE A NERVOUS BREAKDOWN

294
00:11:21,414 --> 00:11:23,049
ON THE WAY TO JAMAICA.

295
00:11:23,049 --> 00:11:26,085
THERE'S NO WAY IN HELL
I WOULDN'T GET ON THIS PLANE.

296
00:11:26,085 --> 00:11:27,153
Yaya: EVERYONE'S GOING
TO TOKYO.

297
00:11:27,153 --> 00:11:29,055
SO WHAT MORE COULD YOU ASK FOR?

298
00:11:29,055 --> 00:11:32,091
BUT BEING IN LUXURY CLASS
IS DEFINITELY, DEFINITELY

299
00:11:32,091 --> 00:11:33,626
THE ICING ON THE CAKE.

300
00:11:35,395 --> 00:11:37,163
Eva: VERY GOOD,
PINK POSITIVE MAKIN' IT

301
00:11:37,163 --> 00:11:38,698
TO TOKYO TOGETHER, BABY.

302
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:41,234
Norelle: AND HOPEFULLY, ONE
OF US MAKES IT TO NUMBER ONE,

303
00:11:41,234 --> 00:11:43,736
AND HOPEFULLY, IT'S US THREE.

304
00:11:43,736 --> 00:11:45,338
Eva: ALL I'VE GOT TO SAY
IS WE GOTTA PROMISE NOT TO GET

305
00:11:45,338 --> 00:11:47,140
BITCHY AND CRITICAL.

306
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,042
Nicole: I DON'T THINK
WE EVER WOULD, THOUGH.

307
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:51,444
Norelle: ALL THREE OF US THAT
ARE, LIKE, PINK POSITIVE BOND.

308
00:11:51,444 --> 00:11:53,046
AND WE ALL TRY
TO HELP EACH OTHER.

309
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:54,547
PINK POSITIVE.

310
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:56,115
All: ♪& WE'RE GOIN' TO TOKYO ♪&

311
00:11:56,115 --> 00:11:57,684
♪& WE'RE GOIN' TO TOKYO ♪&

312
00:11:57,684 --> 00:11:59,986
♪& WE'RE GOIN' TO TOKYO ♪&♪&

313
00:11:59,986 --> 00:12:03,456
Yaya: THEY TOLD ME
I WAS IN LUXURY CLASS.

314
00:12:03,456 --> 00:12:06,292
WHEN WE CHECKED IN
TO THE AMERICAN AIRLINES FLIGHT

315
00:12:06,292 --> 00:12:09,996
TO TOKYO, WE REALIZED WE REALLY
ARE GONNA BE IN TOTALLY

316
00:12:09,996 --> 00:12:11,264
SEPARATE SECTIONS OF THE PLANE.

317
00:12:46,633 --> 00:12:47,767
Ann: WHEN WE GOT OFF
THE FLIGHT,

318
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:49,369
I WAS REALLY RELIEVED.

319
00:12:49,369 --> 00:12:51,537
MY PARENTS ARE GONNA BE
SO PROUD OF ME.

320
00:12:51,537 --> 00:12:53,406
I FELL ASLEEP
AND THEN I WAS FINE.

321
00:12:53,406 --> 00:12:55,341
Norelle: YAY!
Amanda: WHOO!

322
00:12:55,341 --> 00:12:59,045
IT WAS SUCH A LONG FLIGHT,
WE HAD TO CHANGE CLOTHES.

323
00:12:59,045 --> 00:13:01,014
IT WAS A REALLY LONG FLIGHT.

324
00:13:01,014 --> 00:13:02,181
Koko: HELLO.

325
00:13:02,181 --> 00:13:03,750
WHAT'S UP?

326
00:13:03,750 --> 00:13:05,318
WELCOME.

327
00:13:05,318 --> 00:13:06,386
PLEASE COME IN.
Yaya: OKAY.

328
00:13:07,487 --> 00:13:08,655
Koko: WELCOME TO JAPAN.

329
00:13:08,655 --> 00:13:10,223
WELCOME TO TOKYO.

330
00:13:10,223 --> 00:13:12,692
All: (talking at once)

331
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:15,428
Koko: IT'S YOUR FIRST TIME
IN JAPAN?

332
00:13:15,428 --> 00:13:17,130
Nicole: YES.
Koko: YOU GIRLS ARE WELCOME.

333
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,364
IT'S A BEAUTIFUL COUNTRY.

334
00:13:18,364 --> 00:13:20,199
YOU WILL ENJOY IT.

335
00:13:20,199 --> 00:13:21,734
WE JUST GOT INTO TOKYO.

336
00:13:21,734 --> 00:13:24,437
LOOK AT ALL THE BUILDINGS,
IT'S JUST LIKE NEW YORK.

337
00:13:24,437 --> 00:13:27,006
Nicole: IT'S CROWDED
AND VERY HOT.

338
00:13:27,006 --> 00:13:30,176
LIKE, NEW YORK LOOKS LIKE PODUNK
NEXT TO TOKYO.

339
00:13:32,445 --> 00:13:37,083
Yaya: WE'RE DRIVING,
AND WE STOPPED AT THIS SHRINE.

340
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:39,986
Amanda: OH, MY GOODNESS!

341
00:13:39,986 --> 00:13:41,988
Nicole: WOW.

342
00:13:43,122 --> 00:13:44,257
Norelle: OH.

343
00:13:45,992 --> 00:13:47,727
All: (cheer)

344
00:13:47,727 --> 00:13:49,629
Tyra: HELLO.

345
00:13:49,629 --> 00:13:51,064
KONNICHIWA.

346
00:13:51,064 --> 00:13:52,465
All: KONNICHIWA.

347
00:13:52,465 --> 00:13:54,701
Tyra: I BROUGHT YOU HERE
BECAUSE I WANT YOU TO EXPERIENCE

348
00:13:54,701 --> 00:13:59,105
THE MOST AVANT-GARDE
FASHION CAPITAL OF THE WORLD.

349
00:13:59,105 --> 00:14:02,308
IT'S ALSO IMPORTANT FOR MODELS
TO KNOW DIFFERENT CULTURES.

350
00:14:02,308 --> 00:14:05,978
TOKYO IS HOME TO SOME OF THE TOP
FASHION DESIGNERS OF THE WORLD,

351
00:14:05,978 --> 00:14:10,016
TWO OF THEM BEING ISSEY MIYAKE
AND YOHJI YAMAMOTO.

352
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:13,119
TODAY YOU GUYS
ARE AT THE SANNO SHRINE.

353
00:14:13,119 --> 00:14:17,523
THIS PLACE
IS OVER 500 YEARS OLD.

354
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:19,726
WE'RE GONNA DO A RITUAL
CALLED TEMIZUSHA.

355
00:14:19,726 --> 00:14:23,396
IT'S A PURIFICATION OF YOURSELF
BEFORE YOU ASK FOR PROTECTION,

356
00:14:23,396 --> 00:14:26,299
PROSPERITY AND GOOD FORTUNE
FROM THE GODS.

357
00:14:28,134 --> 00:14:30,603
AFTER TEMIZUSHA, YOU'RE SUPPOSED
TO CLAP YOUR HANDS TWICE

358
00:14:30,603 --> 00:14:32,338
AND THEN BOW.

359
00:14:34,307 --> 00:14:36,342
WELCOME TO TOKYO!

360
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:41,280
Eva: I DEFINITELY APPRECIATE
THE CULTURE.

361
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:43,049
I THINK IT'S BEAUTIFUL.

362
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:45,485
AND FOR ME TO BE ABLE
TO EXPERIENCE THIS AND BECOME

363
00:14:45,485 --> 00:14:48,588
MORE WELL-ROUNDED AS A PERSON,
I LOVE IT.

364
00:14:48,588 --> 00:14:50,490
Nicole: THIS IS DEFINITELY
THE TOURISTY AREA.

365
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:52,291
WELCOME TO...

366
00:14:52,291 --> 00:14:55,094
Amanda: HELLO, KITTY.
Norelle: (gasps) AAH!

367
00:14:55,094 --> 00:14:58,564
I WAS SO EXCITED, BECAUSE
THERE'S, LIKE, HELLO KITTY HERE,

368
00:14:58,564 --> 00:15:00,299
WHICH IS MY FAVORITE.

369
00:15:10,643 --> 00:15:13,479
Nicole: WE WALK IN
TO THE HOTEL.

370
00:15:13,479 --> 00:15:17,150
I'M THINKIN' THAT IT'S GONNA BE
SOME SORT OF SPA.

371
00:15:17,150 --> 00:15:18,418
I KNEW IT.

372
00:15:18,418 --> 00:15:21,120
IT'S A SPA.
Eva: OH, WOW.

373
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,555
Ann: ARE THESE OUR BEDS?

374
00:15:22,555 --> 00:15:24,123
Nicole: YEAH.

375
00:15:24,123 --> 00:15:25,124
Norelle: (gasps)

376
00:15:25,124 --> 00:15:26,125
WHAT IS THIS PLACE?

377
00:15:26,125 --> 00:15:28,227
IS THIS OUR HOUSE?

378
00:15:28,227 --> 00:15:30,229
Eva: THIS IS OUR HOTEL?
Ann: YEAH.

379
00:15:30,229 --> 00:15:33,299
Norelle: IT WAS SO WEIRD.

380
00:15:33,299 --> 00:15:35,168
Eva: HOLY MACKEREL.

381
00:15:35,168 --> 00:15:39,138
Amanda: A CAPSULE HOTEL
IS A HOTEL OF CAPSULES--

382
00:15:39,138 --> 00:15:43,209
BASICALLY,
A COFFIN-SIZED CUBICLE.

383
00:15:43,209 --> 00:15:44,477
Eva: IS THIS OUR BED?

384
00:15:44,477 --> 00:15:47,713
Amanda: IT'S KIND OF LIKE
A REALLY CONDENSED YMCA.

385
00:15:47,713 --> 00:15:48,714
Eva: THIS IS OUR HOUSE.

386
00:15:48,714 --> 00:15:50,183
OUR LUGGAGE IS IN THERE,
AND THERE'S

387
00:15:50,183 --> 00:15:51,184
A COMMUNITY BATHROOM.

388
00:15:51,184 --> 00:15:53,319
THIS IS SO OUR HOUSE.

389
00:15:53,319 --> 00:15:56,189
WELL, I ALWAYS WANTED BUNK BEDS
'CAUSE I NEVER HAD A SISTER.

390
00:15:56,189 --> 00:15:57,690
Ann: PINK POSITIVE.

391
00:15:57,690 --> 00:15:59,425
Koko: BEFORE YOU GET INTO
YOUR BED, I HAVE SOMETHING

392
00:15:59,425 --> 00:16:00,993
FOR YOU FROM TYRA.

393
00:16:00,993 --> 00:16:02,562
YES.

394
00:16:02,562 --> 00:16:04,363
Eva: WHERE ARE WE?
IS THIS OUR HOME?

395
00:16:04,363 --> 00:16:07,533
Ann: WHAT THE HELL
DOES THAT SAY?

396
00:16:07,533 --> 00:16:09,302
Eva: "BE READY TO LEAVE
IN 30 MINUTES."

397
00:16:12,605 --> 00:16:15,274
Yaya: WE GET TO THIS GORGEOUS
PLACE WITH A LAKE.

398
00:16:15,274 --> 00:16:17,443
THERE ARE TREES EVERYWHERE.

399
00:16:17,443 --> 00:16:21,481
AND WE GET TO THE ENTRANCEWAY,
THERE IS JAY MANUEL.

400
00:16:21,481 --> 00:16:23,115
All: HEY.

401
00:16:23,115 --> 00:16:25,017
Jay: YOU GUYS DON'T LOOK
SO WORSE FOR THE WEAR.

402
00:16:25,017 --> 00:16:27,186
I KNOW IT'S A LONG FLIGHT
TO THIS PART OF THE WORLD.

403
00:16:27,186 --> 00:16:29,021
AGAIN, TOP MODELS--

404
00:16:29,021 --> 00:16:31,624
THEY FLY AND THEY GOTTA GO
STRAIGHT TO WORK.

405
00:16:31,624 --> 00:16:34,627
I KNOW THIS IS DIFFICULT,
BUT THIS IS THE REAL WORLD.

406
00:16:34,627 --> 00:16:38,164
SO THE OTHER DAY,
YOU GUYS LEARNED ABOUT ACTING.

407
00:16:38,164 --> 00:16:40,566
SO TODAY, WE'RE GONNA
PUT YOUR SKILLS TO THE TEST,

408
00:16:40,566 --> 00:16:43,102
AND YOU GUYS ARE GONNA
HAVE TO DO A COLD READ

409
00:16:43,102 --> 00:16:46,973
FOR A COMMERCIAL
FOR CAMPBELL'S SELECT SOUPS.

410
00:16:46,973 --> 00:16:50,009
NOW, OF COURSE, WE'RE HERE
IN TOKYO, JAPAN.

411
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:53,479
SO YOU GIRLS ARE GOING TO DO
THIS COMMERCIAL IN JAPANESE.

412
00:16:53,479 --> 00:16:56,616
All: (yelling)

413
00:16:56,616 --> 00:16:58,050
Norelle: I CAN BARELY
SPEAK ENGLISH, AND YOU WANT ME

414
00:16:58,050 --> 00:16:59,585
TO SPEAK JAPANESE.

415
00:16:59,585 --> 00:17:01,687
Jay: I'M ACTUALLY GONNA
INTRODUCE YOU GUYS

416
00:17:01,687 --> 00:17:05,156
TO A VERY WELL-KNOWN,
VERY RESPECTED PROMINENT

417
00:17:05,156 --> 00:17:06,726
COMMERCIAL DIRECTOR HERE.

418
00:17:06,726 --> 00:17:10,096
HIS NAME IS MR. ZENTE YOSHIE,
AND HE DOES NOT SPEAK

419
00:17:10,096 --> 00:17:11,631
ANY ENGLISH.

420
00:17:11,631 --> 00:17:13,031
SO HE WILL BE WORKING
WITH AN INTERPRETER.

421
00:17:13,031 --> 00:17:16,402
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

422
00:17:16,402 --> 00:17:19,105
Eva: MR. YOSHIE
SPEAKS NO ENGLISH,

423
00:17:19,105 --> 00:17:21,973
BUT WILL DIRECT US
THROUGH THIS COMMERCIAL

424
00:17:21,973 --> 00:17:24,210
THAT WE WILL DO IN JAPANESE.

425
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:25,278
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

426
00:17:49,702 --> 00:17:51,170
Nicole: THE TRANSLATOR
IS KIND OF LIKE,

427
00:17:51,170 --> 00:17:52,672
"YEAH, YEAH, I SPEAK ENGLISH."

428
00:17:52,672 --> 00:17:53,673
(scoffs)

429
00:17:53,673 --> 00:17:55,441
KINDA.

430
00:17:55,441 --> 00:17:57,577
Jay: SO YOU GUYS HAVE GOT
30 MINUTES TO DO YOUR COMMERCIAL

431
00:17:57,577 --> 00:17:59,378
ONCE THROUGH PERFECTLY.

432
00:17:59,378 --> 00:18:00,513
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

433
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:08,721
Eva: I DON'T SPEAK JAPANESE.

434
00:18:08,721 --> 00:18:10,623
NO.

435
00:18:10,623 --> 00:18:13,292
Nicole: (whispers Japanese)

436
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:22,268
Ann: KONNICHIWA.

437
00:18:22,268 --> 00:18:24,604
Yaya: I'VE BEEN LISTENING
TO PEOPLE SINCE I GOT OFF

438
00:18:24,604 --> 00:18:27,373
THE PLANE, AND HOPEFULLY,
I CAN IMITATE IT AND NOT

439
00:18:27,373 --> 00:18:29,442
EMBARRASS MYSELF TOO MUCH.

440
00:18:29,442 --> 00:18:31,410
I'M JUST TRYING TO REMEMBER
WHAT I READ

441
00:18:31,410 --> 00:18:33,446
BY GOING OVER AND OVER IT.

442
00:18:33,446 --> 00:18:34,580
Jay: WELL, YOU HAVE
CUE CARDS.

443
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:36,282
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

444
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:53,599
Translator: YOU HAVE TO GET
THE BOWL AND SCOOP THE SOUP.

445
00:18:53,599 --> 00:18:55,001
SAY OISHII.

446
00:18:55,001 --> 00:18:56,435
Yaya: OISHII.

447
00:18:56,435 --> 00:18:58,204
Translator: HOLD THE CAN
LIKE THIS,

448
00:18:58,204 --> 00:19:00,006
AND YOU START THE SCRIPT.

449
00:19:00,006 --> 00:19:01,340
Zente: (speaks Japanese)

450
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:05,411
Translator: AFTER YOU HEAR
THE START, YOU CAN START.

451
00:19:05,411 --> 00:19:07,213
Yaya: WHAT'S START
IN JAPANESE?

452
00:19:07,213 --> 00:19:08,314
Zente: START.
Translator: START.

453
00:19:08,314 --> 00:19:09,115
Yaya: OH, OKAY,
