680
00:28:55,701 --> 00:28:58,036
WHAT THE HELL IS THIS STUFF?

681
00:28:58,036 --> 00:28:59,471
LIKE, WHERE DID THEY GET IT?

682
00:28:59,471 --> 00:29:02,274
IT'S LIKE A PICKLED PLUM.

683
00:29:02,274 --> 00:29:04,443
ANTM UMEBOSHI.

684
00:29:04,443 --> 00:29:06,445
Amanda: THE TASTE
CAN'T GET ANY BETTER.

685
00:29:12,551 --> 00:29:15,454
Amanda: IT TASTES SO SWEET
YOU'D SWEAR IT'S CANDY.

686
00:29:15,454 --> 00:29:17,155
Eva: THE TASTE
JUST CAN'T GET ANY BETTER.

687
00:29:22,494 --> 00:29:24,096
Eva: MMM.
Janice: (laughs)

688
00:29:24,096 --> 00:29:27,232
Eva: WITH A TASTE SO SWEET
IT COULD BE CANDY.

689
00:29:27,232 --> 00:29:29,501
ANTM UMEBOSHI.

690
00:29:29,501 --> 00:29:31,069
Norelle: SOMETIMES
EATING HEALTHY FOOD

691
00:29:31,069 --> 00:29:32,437
MEANS EATING YUCKY FOOD.

692
00:29:35,674 --> 00:29:37,109
Norelle: MMM.

693
00:29:37,109 --> 00:29:41,113
ANTEM--ANTM'S "AMEBUSHI"--

694
00:29:41,113 --> 00:29:42,447
Janice: (laughs)

695
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:44,683
Norelle: ANTM'S "AMEBUSHI"
HAS SO MUCH GREAT FLAVOR.

696
00:29:44,683 --> 00:29:45,684
IT'S SO SWEET.

697
00:29:45,684 --> 00:29:47,653
IT'S JUST LIKE EATING CANDY.

698
00:29:47,653 --> 00:29:52,491
Yaya: EACH ANTM UMEBOSHI
IS PACKED WITH FLAVOR,

699
00:29:52,491 --> 00:29:57,095
WITH A TASTE SO SWEET,
YOU'D SWEAR IT'S CANDY.

700
00:29:57,095 --> 00:29:58,764
ANTM UMEBOSHI.

701
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:03,268
Tyra: NOW WE NEED YOU
TO EAT THE PRODUCT,

702
00:30:03,268 --> 00:30:05,470
BECAUSE I'VE NEVER HEARD
OF A GIRL HAVING A COMMERCIAL

703
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:07,139
AND NOT TASTING THE PRODUCT.

704
00:30:07,139 --> 00:30:08,440
Janice: EAT, EAT, EAT!

705
00:30:13,111 --> 00:30:14,713
Yaya: (giggles)

706
00:30:15,981 --> 00:30:17,616
MMM.

707
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:21,553
Yaya: (giggles)

708
00:30:23,121 --> 00:30:25,057
MMM.

709
00:30:25,057 --> 00:30:26,224
(spits)

710
00:30:26,224 --> 00:30:27,225
MMM.

711
00:30:32,097 --> 00:30:34,533
WOW.

712
00:30:34,533 --> 00:30:37,636
NO OFFENSE,
BUT I JUST COULDN'T EAT IT.

713
00:30:37,636 --> 00:30:38,670
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

714
00:30:52,417 --> 00:30:54,319
Tyra: NOW WE NEED YOU
TO EAT THE PRODUCT.

715
00:30:59,591 --> 00:31:01,226
Yaya: (giggles)

716
00:31:01,226 --> 00:31:02,394
MMM.

717
00:31:02,394 --> 00:31:04,196
(spits)

718
00:31:04,196 --> 00:31:08,734
MMM, ANTM's UMEBOSHI
WITH A TASTE SO SWEET

719
00:31:08,734 --> 00:31:11,603
YOU'D SWEAR IT'S CANDY.

720
00:31:11,603 --> 00:31:14,373
I FELT LIKE I WAS GONNA GAG,
AND IT WAS A VERY REACTIONARY

721
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:17,109
KIND OF FLIPPANT DECISION,
LIKE, SPIT IT OUT,

722
00:31:17,109 --> 00:31:18,377
'CAUSE I'M GONNA THROW UP.

723
00:31:18,377 --> 00:31:21,513
RESPECT IS SUCH A BIG THING
HERE IN JAPAN.

724
00:31:21,513 --> 00:31:22,714
I'M SORRY.

725
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:24,383
Janice: WHAT'S IT TASTE LIKE?

726
00:31:24,383 --> 00:31:26,418
Yaya: LIKE NOTHING
I'VE EVER TASTED BEFORE.

727
00:31:26,418 --> 00:31:27,419
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY.

728
00:31:27,419 --> 00:31:28,453
THANKS, YAYA.

729
00:31:28,453 --> 00:31:30,689
Yaya: OKAY, THANK YOU.

730
00:31:30,689 --> 00:31:31,757
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY.

731
00:31:31,757 --> 00:31:34,359
SO FIRST WE HAVE EVA.

732
00:31:34,359 --> 00:31:37,129
EVA, YOU HAD A COMMERCIAL,
AND HERE IS YOUR BEST TAKE.

733
00:31:38,764 --> 00:31:40,565
Eva: AT THIS POINT, NO ONE
EVER KNOWS WHO'S GOIN' HOME.

734
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:41,566
IT COULD BE ME.

735
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:42,534
IT COULD BE AMANDA.

736
00:31:42,534 --> 00:31:43,535
IT COULD BE YAYA.

737
00:31:43,535 --> 00:31:44,536
IT COULD BE BANANA.

738
00:31:44,536 --> 00:31:45,704
YOU NEVER KNOW.

739
00:31:45,704 --> 00:31:47,406
(speaking Japanese)

740
00:31:53,345 --> 00:31:54,646
Eva: CAMPBELL'S SELECTS.

741
00:31:54,646 --> 00:31:56,681
SELECT THE BEST
FROM CAMPBELL'S.

742
00:31:56,681 --> 00:31:58,116
Janice: SHE'S A RAP STAR!

743
00:31:58,116 --> 00:32:00,385
SHE'S A CAMPBELL'S SOUP
RAP STAR, HONEY!

744
00:32:00,385 --> 00:32:02,320
Tyra: EVA, YOU COULDN'T
EVEN GET THE ENGLISH RIGHT.

745
00:32:02,320 --> 00:32:04,456
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

746
00:32:04,456 --> 00:32:09,561
Yuichi: THE LINES,
IT SOUNDS LIKE CHINESE TO US.

747
00:32:09,561 --> 00:32:12,097
Tyra: EVA,
YOU HAD TO SELL UMEBOSHI.

748
00:32:12,097 --> 00:32:13,565
Nigel: I THOUGHT YOU HAD
SOUNDED A LOT BETTER.

749
00:32:13,565 --> 00:32:15,634
ALTHOUGH, OF COURSE, ONCE YOU
GOT THAT STUFF IN YOUR MOUTH,

750
00:32:15,634 --> 00:32:17,035
MY GOODNESS ME, YOU--

751
00:32:17,035 --> 00:32:19,304
Tyra: YOU WERE LIKE...
Eva: OH!

752
00:32:19,304 --> 00:32:20,672
Janice: LIKE CHEWING GUM
IN SCHOOL.

753
00:32:20,672 --> 00:32:22,073
Nigel: BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

754
00:32:22,073 --> 00:32:23,041
YOU PHOTOGRAPH FANTASTICALLY.

755
00:32:23,041 --> 00:32:24,576
VISUALLY,
YOU LOOK BEAUTIFUL.

756
00:32:24,576 --> 00:32:26,478
Tyra: YOUR VOICE IS REALLY
GREAT FOR SELLING PRODUCT.

757
00:32:26,478 --> 00:32:28,013
Nolé: YEAH.

758
00:32:28,013 --> 00:32:29,114
Tyra: ALL RIGHT, EVA, THANKS.

759
00:32:29,114 --> 00:32:31,082
ANN.

760
00:32:31,082 --> 00:32:33,685
WE HAVE YOUR COMMERCIAL
RIGHT HERE.

761
00:32:33,685 --> 00:32:35,287
Ann: (speaking Japanese)

762
00:32:42,594 --> 00:32:44,062
Nolé: I THINK, ANN, YOU NEED
TO LEARN HOW TO HOLD YOUR FACE

763
00:32:44,062 --> 00:32:45,697
A LITTLE BIT MORE PRETTY.

764
00:32:45,697 --> 00:32:48,166
I THINK IN SOME OF THE SPOTS
YOUR FACE WAS A LITTLE ROUGH.

765
00:32:48,166 --> 00:32:49,401
AND YOU ARE A BEAUTIFUL GIRL.

766
00:32:49,401 --> 00:32:52,571
Tyra: THE FACE THING,
YOU WERE DOIN' THIS.

767
00:32:52,571 --> 00:32:54,239
(imitating Ann's Japanese)

768
00:32:54,239 --> 00:32:56,074
Nigel: FOR ME, I THOUGHT
YOU LOOKED FANTASTIC.

769
00:32:56,074 --> 00:32:57,742
I THOUGHT YOU HAD
A LOT OF ENTHUSIASM.

770
00:32:57,742 --> 00:32:59,744
I WAS IMPRESSED
BY THE WAY YOU WENT FOR IT.

771
00:32:59,744 --> 00:33:01,546
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

772
00:33:01,546 --> 00:33:03,114
Yuichi: BASICALLY,
SHE DID VERY WELL.

773
00:33:03,114 --> 00:33:04,583
Tyra: NORELLE.

774
00:33:04,583 --> 00:33:07,085
Norelle: (speaking Japanese)

775
00:33:10,555 --> 00:33:12,057
Norelle: CAMPBELL'S.

776
00:33:12,057 --> 00:33:14,392
SELECT THE BEST
FROM CAMPBELL'S.

777
00:33:14,392 --> 00:33:16,428
Tyra: YOU'RE REALLY GOOD
IN ENGLISH, BUT THE JAPANESE,

778
00:33:16,428 --> 00:33:18,196
CHILD.

779
00:33:18,196 --> 00:33:19,431
Janice: IT'S LIKE
YOU WERE JUST COMING BACK

780
00:33:19,431 --> 00:33:20,432
FROM A NIGHTCLUB.

781
00:33:20,432 --> 00:33:21,533
YOU'D BEEN UP
ALL NIGHT, LIKE,

782
00:33:21,533 --> 00:33:22,968
♪& AH, DE, DE, DE ♪&♪&

783
00:33:22,968 --> 00:33:25,070
YOU KNOW, YOU WEREN'T
DELIVERING IT AT ALL.

784
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:27,339
Nigel: YOU NEED TO MAKE IT AT
LEAST A LITTLE BIT BELIEVABLE.

785
00:33:27,339 --> 00:33:30,141
Tyra: YOU HAD
AN UMEBOSHI COMMERCIAL.

786
00:33:30,141 --> 00:33:31,676
Janice: FINALLY,
YOU HAVE PERSONALITY.

787
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:33,445
YOU WERE BUBBLY, RADIANT.

788
00:33:33,445 --> 00:33:34,613
Tyra: YOU WERE
REALLY CONFIDENT,

789
00:33:34,613 --> 00:33:36,481
AND YOU HAD FUN WITH IT.

790
00:33:36,481 --> 00:33:38,083
ALL RIGHTY,
NEXT WE HAVE AMANDA.

791
00:33:40,051 --> 00:33:42,454
Amanda: (speaking Japanese)

792
00:33:43,722 --> 00:33:45,357
CAMPBELL'S SELECTS.

793
00:33:45,357 --> 00:33:46,224
Tyra: YOU'RE LIKE,
"IS IT OVER? IS IT OVER?

794
00:33:46,224 --> 00:33:48,393
LORD, HELP ME,
PLEASE SAY 'CUT.'"

795
00:33:48,393 --> 00:33:51,229
Amanda: I JUST LOOKED LIKE
A PAIR OF EARS ON AN ONION.

796
00:33:51,229 --> 00:33:52,697
Nolé: I JUST FELT LIKE YOU
WERE JUST SAYING STUFF WITHOUT

797
00:33:52,697 --> 00:33:54,132
ANY PASSION IN BACK OF IT.

798
00:33:54,132 --> 00:33:57,202
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

799
00:33:57,202 --> 00:33:59,371
Yuichi: SHE DIDN'T
MAKE ANY MISTAKES, BUT SHE WAS

800
00:33:59,371 --> 00:34:00,705
A LITTLE BIT TOO FAST.

801
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:02,674
PEOPLE WOULDN'T UNDERSTAND.

802
00:34:02,674 --> 00:34:04,009
Tyra: YAYA.

803
00:34:05,277 --> 00:34:07,546
Yaya: (speaking Japanese)

804
00:34:11,349 --> 00:34:15,487
Janice: IT WAS SO LONG.

805
00:34:15,487 --> 00:34:17,389
Nigel: YOU SOUNDED LIKE
YOU WERE TALKING IN MORSE CODE.

806
00:34:17,389 --> 00:34:19,056
Tyra: YEAH, I THINK YOU WERE
TAKING PAUSES WHEN THERE

807
00:34:19,056 --> 00:34:21,025
WASN'T SUPPOSED TO BE A PAUSE.

808
00:34:21,025 --> 00:34:22,127
Nigel: YOU JUST LOOKED
FANTASTIC.

809
00:34:22,127 --> 00:34:23,695
THAT CAMERA LOVES YOU.

810
00:34:23,695 --> 00:34:25,764
Tyra: SO, YAYA,
YOU HAD UMEBOSHI.

811
00:34:25,764 --> 00:34:26,731
Nolé: YOU SPIT OUT
THE PRODUCT.

812
00:34:26,731 --> 00:34:28,533
THAT MEANS, WHY WERE YOU HERE?

813
00:34:28,533 --> 00:34:31,335
YOU WERE SUPPOSED TO SWALLOW
THAT PRODUCT AS AN ACTRESS.

814
00:34:31,335 --> 00:34:33,538
IT WAS COMPLETELY INSULTING
TO THE CLIENT,

815
00:34:33,538 --> 00:34:34,672
TO THE JAPANESE PEOPLE.

816
00:34:34,672 --> 00:34:36,408
Tyra: THIS IS YOUR ONE SHOT.

817
00:34:36,408 --> 00:34:38,643
AS A MODEL, ESPECIALLY
IF YOU WANT TO BE A TOP MODEL,

818
00:34:38,643 --> 00:34:40,645
YOU GOTTA JUST SUCK IT UP.

819
00:34:40,645 --> 00:34:42,013
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

820
00:34:43,380 --> 00:34:45,183
Yuichi: IT WAS BAD,
REALLY BAD IN FRONT OF CLIENTS

821
00:34:45,183 --> 00:34:48,053
AND CAMERA,
YOU SPIT ON THE PRODUCT.

822
00:34:48,053 --> 00:34:49,688
Yaya: I'M SORRY.

823
00:34:49,688 --> 00:34:51,156
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY.

824
00:34:51,156 --> 00:34:54,426
SO NOW IT'S TIME FOR THE JUDGES
TO DELI--OH.

825
00:34:54,426 --> 00:34:57,094
OH, SORRY.

826
00:34:57,094 --> 00:34:58,463
I'M SORRY.

827
00:34:58,463 --> 00:35:00,498
OH, THERE YOU ARE BEHIND YAYA.

828
00:35:00,498 --> 00:35:01,433
OKAY, COME ON, NICOLE.

829
00:35:01,433 --> 00:35:03,435
I'M SORRY.

830
00:35:03,435 --> 00:35:04,970
SO YOU HAD A COMMERCIAL.

831
00:35:04,970 --> 00:35:08,173
Nicole: (speaking Japanese)

832
00:35:08,173 --> 00:35:09,708
Nolé: YOU LOOKED
VERY CONFUSED.

833
00:35:09,708 --> 00:35:11,743
THE PRODUCT,
YOU WERE SLUMPED OVER.

834
00:35:11,743 --> 00:35:13,979
Janice: YOUR CREAMY SKIN
LOOKED BEAUTIFUL.

835
00:35:13,979 --> 00:35:17,115
YOUR EYES, YOU LOOKED GREAT,
BUT YOUR DELIVERY WASN'T GREAT.

836
00:35:17,115 --> 00:35:19,751
Tyra: OKAY,
YOU HAD TO SELL UMEBOSHI.

837
00:35:19,751 --> 00:35:21,653
Nolé: YOU LOOK BEAUTIFUL
IN PERSON IN FRONT OF ME.

838
00:35:21,653 --> 00:35:24,522
BUT YOU NEED TO REALLY LEARN
MORE OF THE PRODUCT

839
00:35:24,522 --> 00:35:26,157
THAT YOU WERE SELLING
AND REALLY GIVE IT TO ME.

840
00:35:26,157 --> 00:35:27,425
IT REALLY WASN'T THERE.

841
00:35:27,425 --> 00:35:29,127
Tyra: IT'S ALMOST LIKE
I DIDN'T REMEMBER WHEN YOU

842
00:35:29,127 --> 00:35:31,029
FINISHED, NOT MEMORABLE.

843
00:35:31,029 --> 00:35:35,066
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

844
00:35:35,066 --> 00:35:37,335
Yuichi: YOSHIE WASN'T GIVING
YOU MUCH OF DIRECTION,

845
00:35:37,335 --> 00:35:40,605
BUT HOWEVER, YOU HAVE TO MAKE
THE BEST OF WHAT YOU'VE GOT.

846
00:35:40,605 --> 00:35:41,606
Tyra: OKAY.

847
00:35:41,606 --> 00:35:42,607
THANK YOU, NICOLE.

848
00:35:42,607 --> 00:35:44,309
Nicole: THANK YOU.

849
00:35:44,309 --> 00:35:45,377
Tyra: ALL RIGHT,
SO NOW IT'S TIME

850
00:35:45,377 --> 00:35:46,978
FOR THE JUDGES TO DELIBERATE.

851
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:49,114
AND WE WILL CALL YOU BACK
AND DETERMINE WHICH ONE OF YOU

852
00:35:49,114 --> 00:35:50,115
SHOULD BE ELIMINATED.

853
00:35:54,619 --> 00:35:55,987
Tyra: NORELLE.

854
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:57,656
Nolé: NORELLE
ACTUALLY CAME THROUGH FOR ME

855
00:35:57,656 --> 00:35:58,690
IN THE CHALLENGE TODAY.

856
00:35:58,690 --> 00:36:00,258
I WAS REALLY
IMPRESSED WITH HER.

857
00:36:00,258 --> 00:36:01,559
SHE REALLY TOOK IT
TO THE NEXT LEVEL.

858
00:36:01,559 --> 00:36:02,594
Tyra: SHE WAS SO CUTE.

859
00:36:02,594 --> 00:36:04,396
SHE DELIVERED THE LINES
WITH CHUTZPA.

860
00:36:04,396 --> 00:36:05,630
IS THAT A WORD, CHUTZPA?

861
00:36:05,630 --> 00:36:06,731
Nolé: YEAH, OF COURSE.

862
00:36:06,731 --> 00:36:09,000
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

863
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:10,602
Yuichi: SHE'S VERY CHARMING,
BUT THE LINES,

864
00:36:10,602 --> 00:36:12,370
A DIFFICULT THING,
SHE ALWAYS JUST GIVE UP.

865
00:36:12,370 --> 00:36:14,039
Tyra: AMANDA.

866
00:36:14,039 --> 00:36:15,974
Nigel: AMANDA HAS TO GET OVER
THE FACT THAT SHE'S GORGEOUS,

867
00:36:15,974 --> 00:36:17,509
HAS AMAZING BLUE EYES.

868
00:36:17,509 --> 00:36:19,978
SHE DIDN'T SEEM TO HAVE ANY
CONNECTION WITH THE PRODUCT

869
00:36:19,978 --> 00:36:21,179
IN EITHER COMMERCIAL.

870
00:36:21,179 --> 00:36:22,514
Janice: SHE LOOKED
ALIENESQUE.

871
00:36:22,514 --> 00:36:25,316
TO ME, IT DIDN'T REGISTER
COMMERCIAL.

872
00:36:25,316 --> 00:36:27,152
Tyra: I WAS REALLY
DISAPPOINTED TO SEE

873
00:36:27,152 --> 00:36:28,386
HOW DEAD SHE IS.

874
00:36:28,386 --> 00:36:30,388
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

875
00:36:30,388 --> 00:36:33,425
Yuichi: AS EDITORIAL MODELS,
SHE MADE GREAT.

876
00:36:33,425 --> 00:36:36,461
BUT TOO COMMERCIAL,
SHE NEEDED MORE PERSONALITY.

877
00:36:36,461 --> 00:36:38,063
Tyra: ANN.

878
00:36:38,063 --> 00:36:40,065
Janice: TODAY,
SHE WAS LIKEABLE.

879
00:36:40,065 --> 00:36:43,501
I MEAN, SHE WAS LIKEABLE
IN EVEN HER MESS-UPS.

880
00:36:43,501 --> 00:36:46,004
Tyra: THIS IS A BIG SHOCK
TO ME, BECAUSE I THINK ANN

881
00:36:46,004 --> 00:36:48,606
IS KIND OF IN THE GROUP
OF LEADING THE PACK TONIGHT.

882
00:36:48,606 --> 00:36:50,175
YAYA.

883
00:36:50,175 --> 00:36:51,676
Janice: I'VE SEEN BETTER
FACES ON IODINE BOTTLES.

884
00:36:51,676 --> 00:36:53,511
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

885
00:36:53,511 --> 00:36:58,550
Yuichi: GOOD PART OF YAYA
IS SHE'S GOT GREAT PERSONALITY.

886
00:36:58,550 --> 00:37:00,518
Nigel: YAYA LOOKED BEAUTIFUL
WHEN SHE WAS BEING FILMED.

887
00:37:00,518 --> 00:37:02,387
THE CAMERA CERTAINLY LOVES HER.

888
00:37:02,387 --> 00:37:05,223
Nolé: YAYA WAS EXTREMELY
DISAPPOINTING TO ME TODAY.

889
00:37:05,223 --> 00:37:08,193
I FELT THAT SHE SHOULD NEVER
HAVE SPIT THE PRODUCT OUT.

890
00:37:08,193 --> 00:37:09,461
Tyra: THE UMEBOSHI
LITTLE COMMERCIAL

891
00:37:09,461 --> 00:37:12,130
WAS A COUPLE OF SECONDS,
AND SHE DIDN'T EVEN

892
00:37:12,130 --> 00:37:13,665
PULL IT TOGETHER WITH THAT.

893
00:37:13,665 --> 00:37:16,434
AND I FEEL LIKE A LITTLE BIT
OF IT IS POMPOUS WITH HER,

894
00:37:16,434 --> 00:37:19,037
LIKE, "THAT TASTES NASTY,
AND I WASN'T GONNA EAT IT."

895
00:37:19,037 --> 00:37:20,371
Tyra: NICOLE.

896
00:37:20,371 --> 00:37:21,606
Nolé: SHE IS
A VERY PRETTY GIRL.

897
00:37:21,606 --> 00:37:24,109
AND SHE HAS INCREDIBLE
KIND OF MILKY SKIN

898
00:37:24,109 --> 00:37:25,410
AND THIS FIERY RED HAIR.

899
00:37:25,410 --> 00:37:27,746
Zente: (speaking Japanese)

900
00:37:27,746 --> 00:37:29,581
Yuichi: NICOLE IS A VERY
BEAUTIFUL GIRL,

901
00:37:29,581 --> 00:37:34,452
BUT HE WANT MORE,
LIKE SOMETHING--EXPECTED MORE.

902
00:37:34,452 --> 00:37:37,055
Tyra: NICOLE IS BLAH WHEN IT
COMES TO REALLY CONNECTING

903
00:37:37,055 --> 00:37:39,023
TO A VERY BROAD AUDIENCE.

904
00:37:39,023 --> 00:37:40,525
Janice: SHE'S BEYOND BLAH.

905
00:37:40,525 --> 00:37:42,026
Nigel: I THINK NICOLE
REALLY DOES NEED

906
00:37:42,026 --> 00:37:43,194
AN OUT-OF-BODY EXPERIENCE.

907
00:37:43,194 --> 00:37:44,429
IT WAS JUST A VERY MUCH
A FLAT LINE.

908
00:37:44,429 --> 00:37:46,064
Tyra: EVA.

909
00:37:46,064 --> 00:37:47,532
Nolé: IN YOUR COMMERCIAL,
SHE WAS AN ABSOLUTE

910
00:37:47,532 --> 00:37:49,167
TOKYO DISASTER.

911
00:37:49,167 --> 00:37:50,201
Tyra: SHE WAS A TYPHOON.

912
00:37:50,201 --> 00:37:52,070
